{"id": "EUVD-2026-76603", "enisaUuid": "522f4677-50e7-344c-9b26-d1c86f90970a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: clear opcnt on compound arg release to prevent OOB read\n\nnfsd4_release_compoundargs() resets args->ops to the inline iops[8]\narray when the dynamically-allocated ops buffer is freed, but leaves\nargs->opcnt at its original value (which can be up to 200 for NFSv4.1+\ncompounds).\n\nIf rq_status_counter is stuck at an odd value (which can happen when\nnfsd_dispatch() hits an error path after setting it odd), the RPC\nstatus dumpit handler reads min(opcnt, 16) entries from args->ops[].\nSince iops only has 8 elements and is the last field in struct\nnfsd4_compoundargs, reading indices 8-15 accesses adjacent slab memory\nand leaks it to userspace via netlink.\n\nZero opcnt unconditionally in nfsd4_release_compoundargs() so stale\ncompound metadata is never exposed through the status interface.\n\n[ cel: Remove the kvfree_rcu_mightsleep() sleep from the exposure window ]", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:51:04", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58bcdfb2b2e412088839ae740b1a95154dc0b8d0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e879148867bd4c4cac42e063ffaffa187dddc6fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1a4f7b1848f95302df598217e1c7a1410c2d0c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae4c38555e81563b8dc5eae55ffd70f0ea97aa5a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89691", "GHSA-v764-gh88-p9gg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "087a9f8d-0c65-34bc-b0e1-183e5e891e4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2bdda2c4-6453-369f-ae89-4c79d57d32cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "4420305f-08e8-398f-92dc-0c1d79427b18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd9d6a3efa9709e653aafbeb859289feccb8e70c <58bcdfb2b2e412088839ae740b1a95154dc0b8d0"}, {"id": "50c87c45-9ba6-3bd6-9214-d06a96501f85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "7a62a2ef-6826-3a05-98a3-283cde2edb0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd9d6a3efa9709e653aafbeb859289feccb8e70c <e879148867bd4c4cac42e063ffaffa187dddc6fe"}, {"id": "8da213bc-332a-371f-8907-f85ccd8eae83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd9d6a3efa9709e653aafbeb859289feccb8e70c <ae4c38555e81563b8dc5eae55ffd70f0ea97aa5a"}, {"id": "90d1aa16-c12c-3a06-8303-af050ba826d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a70d26ad-fd38-3436-aedd-4e7c77bdd9a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "a7b08426-0332-3b43-a1a1-046e0f1e25bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bd9d6a3efa9709e653aafbeb859289feccb8e70c <c1a4f7b1848f95302df598217e1c7a1410c2d0c5"}, {"id": "afe98f56-c9f3-3488-bab5-3edab6ce5971", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9655a229-75fe-350d-bebd-c33365c8d415", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}